            <ArticleTitle>Medullary nephrocalcinosis in idiopathic hypercalciuria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1903-1904</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1189</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Idiopathic hypercalciuria is a metabolic abnormality characterized by excessive calcium excretion in the urine with normal serum calcium levels and is a common risk factor for formation of kidney stones and/or nephrocalcinosis. These patients benefit from a normal-calcium, reduced-animal protein, and low-salt diet, along with a thiazide diuretic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
